                     |   monitoring)        |                      |\n| - TigerGraph         |   split (Cypher /    |                      | - GitHub stargazer   |                      |\n|   (GSQL only, $970+) |   SPARQL / SQL %)    |                      |   scan (neo4j,       |                      |\n| - Self-host          |   → tells which      |                      |   supabase, dgraph)  |                      |\n|   (PostgreSQL +      |   languages matter   |                      | - SEO /comparison    |                      |\n|   pgvector + custom) | - Free → Paid 30d    |                      |   page (vs Neptune,  |                      |\n| - Memgraph           |   conversion rate    |                      |   vs Neo4j, vs       |                      |\n|   ($25, Cypher only) |   (target >5%)       |                      |   TigerGraph)        |                      |\n|                      | - LTV:CAC (target    |                      |                      |                      |\n|                      |   >16×)              |                      |                      |                      |\n+----------------------+----------------------+----------------------+----------------------+                      |\n| Cost Structure                              | Revenue Streams                                                     |\n+---------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| Fixed: ~¥40,000/mo                          | Subscription: ¥0 / ¥1,980 / ¥4,980 / ¥98,000 / ¥1,000,000+         |\n| - Vultr $241                                |                                                                     |\n| - B2 ~$10                                   | Overage:                                                            |\n| - CF Workers $5                             | - Storage ¥10/GB-month (85% margin)                                 |\n| - Domain / monitor ~$20                     | - Compute ¥300/QCU-hour (98% margin)                                |\n|                                             | - MCP ¥3/100 calls (99.5% margin, moat)                             |\n| Variable:                                   | - OWL DL ¥500/run (98% margin)                                      |\n| - Stripe 2.9% + ¥30                         |                                                                     |\n| - Murakumo electricity (low)                | Pro tier break-even: 9 paid tenants                                 |\n+---------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. Unit Economics Summary\n\n### 9.1 Cost per tenant\n\n| Tenant type | Cost component | Monthly ¥ |\n|---|---|---|\n| Free | RW share (1/200 tenant) + 1 GB B2 + edge | ~¥1,800 (acquisition cost) |\n| Starter | RW share (1/100) + 10 GB B2 + edge + MCP | ~¥500 |\n| Pro | RW share (1/50) + 100 GB B2 + edge + MCP + OWL | ~¥750 |\n| Business | RW share (1/5) + 1 TB B2 + dedicated MVs | ~¥10,000 |\n| Enterprise | dedicated RW node + custom | ~¥150,000+ |\n\n### 9.2 Gross margin\n\n| Tier | Price | Cost | Gross margin |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Free | ¥0 | ¥1,800 | -∞ (acquisition) |\n| Starter | ¥1,980 | ¥500 | 75% |\n| **Pro** | **¥4,980** | **¥750** | **85%** ← target |\n| Business | ¥98,000 | ¥10,000 | 90% |\n| Enterprise | ¥1,000,000+ | ¥150,000+ | 85%+ |\n\n### 9.3 Break-even\n\nFixed cost ¥40,000/mo. Pro が 9 件で break-even (¥4,980 × 9 = ¥44,820 > ¥40,000)。Free tenant の acquisition cost を吸収するには Pro 比 20% conversion 仮定で **Pro 20 件 + Free 80 件** が安定点。\n\n### 9.4 LTV:CAC target\n\n- CAC target: **< ¥3,000** (autonomous agent driven channel: HN cron, MCP listing, GitHub scan — 人件費ほぼ 0、Murakumo self-host で variable cost も 0)\n- LTV target: **> ¥48,000** (Pro avg lifetime 12 mo × ¥4,980 × 85% margin × 1.2 overage uplift)\n- **LTV:CAC = 16×** (SaaS healthy line は 3×、我々は autonomous channel で 16×)\n\n---\n\n## 10. Competitive Moat Analysis (minimax stable equilibrium)\n\n3 つの moat が形成する **stable equilibrium**: regret matrix の全 scenario に対して同時崩壊しない構造。\n\n### 10.1 Moat 1: MCP-first architecture\n\n- 競合状況: Neo4j / Neptune / TigerGraph / Memgraph / Stardog いずれも native MCP なし\n- 模倣難度: **High** — MCP endpoint を後付けすると認証 (DID native) / streaming / OWL の semantic mapping を再設計する必要があり、既存 graph DB の architecture に fundamental change\n- 持続期間 estimate: 12-24 months (Neptune が MCP 追加するには re:Invent サイクル必要)\n\n### 10.2 Moat 2: Multi-language (Cypher + SPARQL + SQL)\n\n| 競合 | Cypher | SPARQL | SQL |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Neo4j | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ |\n| Neptune | ✓ (openCypher) | ✓ | ✗ |\n| TigerGraph | ✗ (GSQL only) | ✗ | ✗ |\n| Stardog | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ |\n| **yatabase** | **✓** | **✓** | **✓** |\n\n模倣難度: **Very High** — Kotoba/Datomic 上に 3 wire を統一実装する必要。Neo4j は SPARQL を加えるのに RDF triple store を新規構築せねばならず、3-5 年プロジェクト。\n\n### 10.3 Moat 3: BWA $0 egress\n\n- B2 の Bandwidth Alliance (Cloudflare 経由 egress 無料) は **Backblaze + Cloudflare partnership に依存**\n- AWS / GCP / Azure には等価 partnership 存在しない\n- 模倣難度: **Structurally Impossible** — Neptune は AWS egress $0.09/GB から逃れられない (AWS itself にとって自社 egress fee は revenue source)\n\n### 10.4 Minimax stable equilibrium\n\n3 moats を §1.4 regret matrix の各 scenario で評価:\n\n| Scenario | Moat 1 (MCP) | Moat 2 (multi-lang) | Moat 3 (BWA) | Stable? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A: Neo4j → $30 | 残存 | 残存 | 残存 | ✓ |\n| B: Neptune adds MCP | 部分浸食 | 残存 (Cypher 追加困難) | 残存 | ✓ |\n| C: Memgraph → $15 | 残存 | 残存 | 残存 | ✓ |\n| D: Supabase graph 追加 | 残存 | 部分浸食 (SQL は被る) | 残存 | ✓ |\n| E: Baseline | 全残存 | 全残存 | 全残存 | ✓ |\n\n→ **3 moats のうち 1 つが浸食されても他 2 つで防衛可能**。これが minimax stable equilibrium の定義。\n\n---\n\n## 11. Sprint 1 update (2026-05-21)\n\nADR-2605190000 §4 (Sprint 1 hypotheses) の進捗を更新:\n\n### H1: MCP listing → 5× signup (in progress)\n\n- Status: **進行中 (2026-05-21)**\n- 完了: mcpservers.org へ「Yatabase」として申請済み — review within 12h\n- 進行中: awesome-mcp-servers PR (fork: com-junkawasaki:add-yatabase) — Jun が GitHub で手動 PR 作成待ち\n- 残: Cursor MCP registry / Claude Desktop official registry への申請\n- Next action: awesome-mcp-servers PR マージ後に `BMC_H1_SUBMITTED=true` を K8s env var に設定\n\n### H2: LP positioning shift (graph DB BaaS only)\n\n- Status: **完了 2026-05-21**\n- Commits: `61911043fdc` (initial graph-only pivot), `f728116b` (minimax 5-tier pricing full LP)\n- 変更:\n  - S3-compatible object storage messaging を LP から削除、graph DB BaaS に positioning 集約\n  - Hero: \"The only graph DB your AI agents can query.\"\n  - 5-tier plan grid (Free / Starter ¥1,980 / Pro ¥4,980 / Business ¥98,000 / Enterprise)\n  - Overage table (Storage ¥10/GB, Compute ¥300/QCU-hr, MCP ¥3/100, OWL DL ¥500, Egress ¥0)\n  - 10-row competitor comparison incl. OWL reasoning + CPU-time billing rows\n  - Moat/Unique/Core badges on feature cards\n  - Protocol strip showing Cypher + SPARQL + SQL inline queries\n- 検証: pending — LP traffic の bounce rate / time-on-page を 7 日後 (2026-05-28) に測定\n\n### H3 (new): \"S3 BaaS\" search intent loss risk\n\n- 仮説: LP から S3 messaging を削除したことで \"S3 alternative\" 検索流入が失われる可能性\n- 対策案: `/storage` 比較 page を別途用意し、yatabase は graph DB として positioning しつつ S3 互換 endpoint は無料提供と明示する (graph state の中で blob を保持)\n- 判定基準: 2026-05-28 までに organic search traffic が 50% 以上落ちたら `/storage` page を緊急公開、それ以下なら graph 集中継続\n- Owner: yatabase agent (autonomous)\n\n### H4 (new): MCP-first messaging A/B\n\n- LP headline candidates:\n  - A: \"The only graph DB your AI agents can query directly\" (current)\n  - B: \"Cypher + SPARQL + SQL + MCP in one DB, $33/mo\"\n  - C: \"$0 egress graph DB for AI agents\"\n- Sprint 2 で 3-way A/B test (Cloudflare A/B feature)、conversion rate 最大の copy を 2026-06-04 に確定\n\n---\n\n## 12. 結論と次の判断点\n\n1. **Pro tier は ¥4,980/mo (≒ $33) で minimax 最適** — 据置確定\n2. **Storage ¥10/GB-month, Compute ¥300/QCU-hour, MCP ¥3/100 calls** が overage minimax\n3. **3 moats (MCP-first, multi-language, BWA $0 egress) が stable equilibrium** を形成\n4. **LP positioning は graph DB BaaS に集約完了**、object storage は別 page に退避検討\n5. **Break-even は Pro 9 件 / 月**、LTV:CAC 16× は autonomous channel で達成可能\n6. 次の判断点: 2026-05-28 LP traffic 計測 → H3 (S3 search intent) の判定、2026-05-22 MCP listing 申請、2026-06-04 LP A/B winner 確定\n\n本 ADR は ADR-2605190000 を supersede し、yatabase の価格・positioning・BMC の SSoT として運用する。次回見直しは 2026-08-21 (3 ヶ月後) または competitor structural shock (§1.3 scenario A-D 発生時) のいずれか早い方。\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605210001-yatabase-minimax-pricing-bmc.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "yatabase-product-bmc", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-21", :adr/date "2026-05-21", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["adr-2605190000-yatabase-bmc-lean" "adr-2605080000-yatabase-yata-retail-cloud" "adr-2605180000-lawfirm-product-focus-bmc-lean"], :adr/authoritative_for ["yatabase graph DB BaaS 価格設計 (minimax)" "yatabase storage / compute 単価" "yatabase Business Model Canvas (2026-05-21 改訂)" "yatabase Lean Canvas (2026-05-21 改訂)"], :adr/supersedes ["adr-2605190000-yatabase-bmc-lean"]}]
